      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AUTOMATIC MAN (7) sets the standard off a debut third at Pinjarra Scarpside, where he was unwanted in the market but worked home evenly to be beaten a length in a Mdn over 1300m. He resumes after five months and the winning Albany trial gives him the right platform to convert that promise. HOLD MY WINE (1) is the main danger, dropping out of CL2 company after a fifth at Kalgoorlie that had merit given he was held up from the 100m and was beaten just under two lengths. Finds a winnable race. DOLCE MASCHINO (2) also gets class relief from a Class 1, and the first-up fifth at this track can be treated a shade better after a bump at the start. QUEEN CARTEL (4) was poor last start, but her previous third at this track, beaten just over half a length at long odds, keeps her in the mix as a place-to-win chance if she recaptures that run. TRADINGS OVER (8) trialled well here recently and is not to be discounted on debut.",
